# Hades II (Supergiant Games 2025: their own engine on The Forge, DirectX 12 only, through VKD3D-Proton; Lua 5.2, SDL2)
# summary: 4K High, VSync at 60 with the GPU ~30% busy (Borderless in the game's settings), no driver busy-wait
# Proton Experimental (the default). Measured 2026-10-20 at 3840x2160, Graphics Quality High (the highest), VSync on:
# 59.9 fps at the main menu, in the Crossroads and in two minutes of non-stop attacks and casts in the Training
# Grounds (lowest 59.4), GPU 16-31% busy. Steam Input is not forced for this game (Opted-in Controller Mask 1000),
# so Proton hands controllers to the game itself (SDL2).
# NVIDIA's driver (615) busy-waits for each present: VKD3D-Proton's vkd3d-swapchain thread spun a whole core (99%) in
# libnvidia-glcore's atomics. __GL_YIELD=USLEEP makes the driver sleep there instead: the thread drops to 3% and the
# game process from 184% to 62% of a core, at the same 59.9 fps.
__GL_YIELD=USLEEP
